Elliot: small UX catch from today's QA — the docs side panel labels the flow as 'Route settings' but the main docs page and our glossary use 'Endpoint settings'. feels inconsistent.
Nina (Docs): thanks — where exactly? can you paste the panel path?
Elliot: Console > Network > Routes list > settings (side panel opens on right). header says 'Route settings' and the first paragraph uses 'route' repeatedly. main doc title is 'Endpoint settings' and examples call them endpoints.
Sam - Eng: this will affect our anchor slugging when we generate deep links. our autolinker looks for canonical headings; mismatch may cause 404-style in-panel links.
Nina (Docs): proposal: adopt 'endpoint' as canonical in docs and console. update side panel copy to 'Endpoint settings' and add a one-line alias line in docs: "Note: some screens use the term 'route'" for a transition window.
Priya (A11y): accessibility note: when the side panel contains crosslinks that jump to the doc, we need to ensure screen-readers get a notification and focus is managed. currently clicking a link mutates the hash but SR doesn't announce. also keyboard users lose context if the side panel doesn't close or set aria-hidden.
Sam - Eng: plan for dev: when link clicked -> close side panel, set aria-hidden=true on panel, update hash, then focus the target heading with tabindex=-1 and focus(). add a short timeout so the SPA settles. snippet we'll add to PR: 
```
sidePanel.close();
panel.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
setTimeout(() => {
  const target = document.getElementById(targetId);
  if (target) {
    target.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
    target.focus();
    history.replaceState(null, '', `#${targetId}`);
  }
}, 120);
```
Nina (Docs): i'll update the heading slugs and add an anchor for the side panel to point to, plus an alias line at top of the article: "Terminology: endpoint (previously referred to as route)". i'll also submit a mapping doc of pages where 'route' appears so we can batch-change.
Elliot: one more UX ask — can we add a tiny link icon next to section headers inside the panel that opens the docs at the right section? users expect quick jumps.
Sam - Eng: yes. Q: should that icon open the docs in a new tab or reuse the same tab? current side panel links go same-tab.
Priya (A11y): same-tab preferred if we manage focus properly. if we do open new tab, aria-label should say '(opens in new tab)' and we must include rel=noopener. for keyboard users add a visible focus state on the icon.
Nina (Docs): i'll write two copy options and recommend same-tab with focus landing. i'll also check the help-center search alias list so people searching for 'route' still find 'endpoint'.
Elliot: can someone create a tiny ticket with acceptance criteria: 1) change panel header copy; 2) docs alias line; 3) add deep-link icon in panel; 4) focus + aria-hidden behavior; 5) analytics event for link clicks.
Sam - Eng: I'll file ticket INFRA-3078 and include unit tests for focus behavior plus e2e for the deep link flow.
infra-bot: created INFRA-3078: "Console side panel term harmonization + deep-link/a11y fixes" assigned to Sam - Eng, due 7 days.
Nina (Docs): thanks — i'll follow up with a PR for copy and the list of 'route' occurrences.
Elliot: great, thanks everyone :thumbsup:
